maintainer (1.1.2-1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Privileged actions now actually prompt for a password. No D-Bus bus
    policy or systemd unit was shipped for the helper, so calls were
    rejected before Polkit could be consulted. Both are now installed, and
    a bus-level rejection is reported as the configuration fault it is.
  * Irreversible actions (terminate process, vacuum journal) require the
    password on every attempt; reversible or read-only actions (clean
    package cache, refresh SMART) no longer prompt for an active session.
  * Fix update classification for Linux Mint and case-sensitive security
    origins, so Mint-native packages and Debian-Security updates are no
    longer misclassified.
  * Disclose kernel updates and reboot-required state on the Updates page.
  * Add a Security Only / Everything selection mode with a top action bar,
    status icons per package, and per-package selection that re-plans
    through apt's own dependency resolver rather than a client-side filter.
  * Style the new Updates controls in both themes; clarify the Custom
    selection state with a visible indicator.

 -- Maintainer Developers <maintainer@maintainerapp.io>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000

maintainer (1.1.0-1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Ship the full interface: eight pages, device specifications, hardware
    inventory, expanded diagnostics and cleanup flows, and the complete
    stylesheets. The 1.0.0 package was built before this work was committed
    and contained the earlier scaffold interface.
  * Refresh only the page currently on screen, restoring the idle CPU
    reduction that the scaffold build had.
  * Cache hwmon topology so a sample reads only sensor values.

 -- Maintainer Developers <maintainer@maintainerapp.io>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

